tools.description:
Create a complete page from a declarative structure. Accepts builder-specific widget definitions and creates the page with all elements in one call. Returns page_id, edit_url, and preview_url.

Nested structure shape (Divi 5 / any builder that nests): use `children: [...]` at every container level. As of plugin v7.0.32 the Divi builder also accepts `rows / cols / columns / modules / elements / innerBlocks` as aliases for `children` (Divi-vocabulary; soft warning surfaces in the response trace). Canonical example for a Divi 5 hero:

```
structure: [{
  type: "section",
  settings: { background_color: "#1f4e7a", padding: "120px|0|120px|0" },
  children: [{
    type: "row",
    children: [{
      type: "column",
      children: [
        { type: "heading", settings: { title: "Hello", tag: "h1" } },
        { type: "text",    settings: { content: "<p>Para</p>" } }
      ]
    }]
  }]
}]
```

Flat shape also works — pass leaf modules at the top level and the builder auto-wraps them in section > row > column. Plugin v7.0.32 hard-errors with `respira_children_dropped` (HTTP 500) if any container payload declares children but the emit produced fewer innerBlocks, so silent data-loss is no longer possible.
